==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|merciful}}, {{m|enm|mercyful}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|mercy|ful|pos=adjective}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|mildheort}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɜːsɪfl̩/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɝsɪfl̩/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-merciful.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|mer|ci|ful}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Showing [[mercy]].
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|passage=`Listen, Holly. Thou art a good and honest man, and I fain would spare thee; but, oh! it is so hard for woman to be '''merciful'''.'}}
#* {{RQ:Chesnutt House Behind the Cedars|I|passage=The murderer, he recalled, had been tried and sentenced to imprisonment for life, but was pardoned by a '''merciful''' governor after serving a year of his sentence.}}

